  "conclusion": "Original Zeitauktion specimen 2503540 identifies exact 79280P. Full photographs 4, 11 and 14 were inspected: black Arabic-numbered Prince Date chronograph dial and steel tachymeter bezel; closed Tudor/Geneva/Suisse shield back; opened movement with Tudor-signed rotor and readable 7750 plate marking beside the balance. The strap is a Zeitauktion-branded replacement leather strap, not proof of original Tudor bracelet or buckle execution. Photographs are representative of this black-dial specimen only. No suffix stripping, neighbouring 79280/79260/79270 equivalence, supplier revision or component interchangeability is inferred. No inner-back or between-lug reference engraving is shown. Dealer approximate 2007 dates this specimen, not the full production interval or user watch. Source condition, service and pressure-test claims do not establish the user watch condition, authenticity, originality, water resistance or warranty. Packaging, register sheet, pressure slip and workshop collage are excluded. Original bracelet/clasp and inner-back photographs remain gaps.",
